# Line-ending policy.
#
# The repository stores text as LF. `text=auto` lets git normalise on the way
# in, so a Windows checkout can keep CRLF on disk without every file showing
# as modified. Binary assets are marked explicitly rather than left to content
# detection, which can misfire on small files.

* text=auto

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Files that must stay LF on every platform: shell scripts break with CRLF,
# and the manifest is served verbatim.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.webmanifest text eol=lf
